{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PLpns12BVQ1f346gvqn9zH","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-61-btgqapmg/.xorq/scripts/build_metric.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"}),\n)\n\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"}),\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets\ntotal_fm = fm.aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population (SUMLEV=10)\nus_pop = (census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 10)\n          .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n          .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and compute metric\nexpr = (\n    total_fm.join(us_pop, total_fm.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_fm.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select('total_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! So:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- Total U.S. population (2025): 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to create a script that will join these two datasets and calculate the ratio per 100,000 residents. I'll create a build script that:\n1. Gets the total farmers markets from farmers_markets\n2. Gets the US population from census (where SUMLEV=10)\n3. Calculates the metric","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PLpns12BVQ1f346gvqn9zH","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-61-btgqapmg/.xorq/scripts/build_metric.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"}),\n)\n\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"}),\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets\ntotal_fm = fm.aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population (SUMLEV=10)\nus_pop = (census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 10)\n          .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n          .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and compute metric\nexpr = (\n    total_fm.join(us_pop, total_fm.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_fm.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select('total_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic",